0..63 Comment "// One ascription path for a module and a theory: a module is a"
64..137 Comment "// model of a theory, `module M : Model(T)` ascribes it transparently and"
138..212 Comment "// `module M :> Model(T)` seals it, the theory\'s sorts abstract outside. A"
213..284 Comment "// theory with no laws is an ML signature; the same ascription checks a"
285..361 Comment "// theory with laws, whose members are the module\'s proofs. After Kaposi and"
362..427 Comment "// Xie (_Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories_, FSCD 2024,"
428..495 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10), whose first-order models are a"
496..566 Comment "// theory\'s algebras, and Rossberg, Russo and Dreyer (_F-ing Modules_,"
567..634 Comment "// doi:10.1017/S0956796814000264) for sealing as opaque ascription."
635..637 Comment "//"
638..652 Comment "// - see: #746"
